The concern is confirmed, and there is a second executable-contract gap: the profile requires every trusted component to remain unchanged until the last domain member exits, but the authoritative phase list re-verifies identity before domain teardown, and the manager re-verifies only a subset of the TCB. These are specification rework items, not an external blocker, so the correct verdict branch will be changes requested → `to-dev`.
